      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/man-la-yahduruhu-al-faqih:4:19:9",
      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/19/5159",
      "text": [
        " اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ\n۝ أَنَّهُ مَنْ قَتَلَ نَفْساً بِغَيْرِ نَفْسٍ أَوْ فَسٰادٍ فِي اَلْأَرْضِ فَكَأَنَّمٰا قَتَلَ اَلنّٰاسَ جَمِيعاً  ۝\nقَالَ \"هُوَ وَادٍ فِي جَهَنَّمَ لَوْ قَتَلَ اَلنَّاسَ جَمِيعاً كَانَ فِيهِ وَ لَوْ قَتَلَ نَفْساً وَاحِدَةً كَانَ فِيهِ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5159 - It is narrated from Hanan ibn Sadir from Abu Abdullah (as) regarding the saying of Allah (swt), the Almighty and Majestic:\n\"Whoever kills a soul without [the soul having killed] another soul or [without causing] corruption on the earth, it is as if he had killed all mankind\" (Surah Al-Ma'idah 5:32).\nImam (as) said: \"It is a valley in Hell; if a person were to kill all of mankind, he would be in it, and if he were to kill just one soul, he would still be in it.\""
        ]
      }
    },
